# .npmrc — settings applied to every `npm install` in this project.
#
# Default registry: the npmmirror (China) mirror, so domestic users can
# `git clone && npm install` without extra config. Anyone on a faster /
# official link can override per-shell without editing this file, e.g.:
#
#   npm install --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org
#
# Binary toolchain mirrors (electron / electron-builder / sharp / sass /
# phantomjs / chromedriver) are NOT configured here — modern npm no
# longer recognises the old `electron_mirror=` etc. keys, and the
# `npm_config_*` env-var form is npm-only (the actual download scripts
# don't read it). `scripts/install.js` injects the right env vars
# before spawning any postinstall step that needs them.
#
# What we set here:
#   - registry: defaults to npmmirror, can be overridden with --registry
#   - skip the noisy "fund" / "audit" announcements
#   - use the lockfile as the authoritative source of truth (`package-lock=true`)
#   - bump fetch timeouts so a slow link gets a real error, not a silent hang
#   - force `legacy-peer-deps` so a future transitive bump doesn't break us

registry=https://registry.npmmirror.com

fund=false
audit=false
package-lock=true
fetch-timeout=180000
fetch-retries=5
fetch-retry-mintimeout=20000
fetch-retry-maxtimeout=120000
legacy-peer-deps=true
